wess, did not feel any pain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.809,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"77fa2eb413f87141e77997af261fd1cc972241f110a41e914bfe10d3cbda88bd","compact":"85de5e3cee9003d9a326176d299c5b6810471205798e5e87b15fbfbff326f1a8","nasal":"85de5e3cee9003d9a326176d299c5b6810471205798e5e87b15fbfbff326f1a8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":13,"english":"That impetuous one incapable of being conquered, summoning his utmost vehemence, rushing on, pealt a slap at his* mighty elephant. *Mahodara's.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.216,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"194ecb4a8c84409882a79ffa1e54806b213f07a59a2c0f8e91a1975f8c2551c6","compact":"a24e550103d0eb546ab7934ae2cb816da877fcd9cd9ceb9d5949a2337b08d0ec","nasal":"c2468e236ddd49c698c02c55dc64daa50b9fa45fbaf4bb476aadbdf2bc7a8f44"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":14,"english":"Then pulling out his tusks, the highly powerful son of Vāli, darting against Devāntaka, dealt him a blow therewith in that encounter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eefcc093c85d961c5d32c9c202b22d4bb824b83aad12e9cb1fd7260f52d559cb","compact":"0da220776830c161b238e4844536d007d90163dd01445f80336bb285051c01f9","nasal":"accb4d0e2d6c7eabc2fd91b3cdc4aa6fd1bc013c545e5e8c23c5f717a549c2f4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga"