 riven and was stupefied by that exceedingly powerful one.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.824,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058026","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7c5631ce07bae5ff2500bfd781c7ddd20706441bb5a351dc33493bf58ea8fe1d","compact":"a88d20915b4c4b8290e5511ebc0d045107a043a7751bbe1f9862e4dcb78d4086","nasal":"95aa299c52a9249277fd49c6a887015150b7d43ef02c9c1c056527464e6a3cd5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-27","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":27,"english":"Then that (monkey) possessed of tremendous vehemence, having regained his senses, uprooting a crag with a whole tract of trees, struck it at Mahodara's head.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.607,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058027","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"12b94a7965175af904e61bb854d98bc1883eb4277199cff3cf011b06af765194","compact":"dbe41d0ac46df8df1e361ec9cc504b09f6739e19b98958ac585493df1d8f24b7","nasal":"3b70b45ac3a06e3948e3647ec8c82b3cd195fd081d3f68731a0b8de2addb374c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-28","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":28,"english":"Struck by that mighty enemy, Mahodara, broken down by the impetus of that rock, deprived of his senses, dropped down dead on the ground, like a cliff smite with the thunderbolt.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.6,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058028","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"395dcb092e39a2c9335abb98addb86fbbb1104ac2b89cf8ff3cfb96c3bceace1","compact":"2c3598fc72dbbaf1fb41868bc6551c321ad4253986cc847b5145f4215654577b","nasal":"2c3598fc72dbbaf1fb41868bc6551c321ad4253986cc847b5145f4215654577b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-29","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":29,"english":"Seeing his uncle slain, Triſiras took up his bow; and inflamed with fury pierced Hanumān with whetted arrows.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058029","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ada056336bd0e16ac0673fc1cbe1deb73e22c5a2428e639efac3f19b7cf38def","compact":"bed9a0783e8dc0fcb4fdb3d5e542f7cf6205c1bd8e8804d3884005cb3d58fb28","nasal":"7d0a8d442038a989335a56fd8d2217ccf08e3a42019e4c860bceebe4a89356bb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-30","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":30,"english":"Then Hanumān flying into a fury, bounding to the welkin, with his nails ript the steed of Triớiras, even as a lion cleave a powerful elephant.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.697,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058030","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"be24f75aaecec87b7cf10d9306a824d3b666e54300cbd1c4bd3fe0a8b7f6c40d","compact":"ec99ed83fae1faba6874ebdf081978bcf1a1b7c3097bf9400b39949a1b60d1b7","nasal":"572b53128f8e91b43fe091447cb4d34784b1065dbd87cda170790d30e0fa3f1e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-31","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":31,"english":"Then taking a dart even as the destroyer employ the fatal night, Ravana's son, TriSiras discharged it at the offspring of the wind-god.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058031","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e56f46d9a2184fceeda551452f8e10154ee5ee738e26c30738008df377ce193b","compact":"bbedcd2e732bed74bf6d7c86ccec60a41c4b71b0ea1444eee523d91984228d26","nasal":"a26817b55f8e0dfa1038486eff68dc69925d6f49b31ea87064eec8e71fa336af"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-32","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":32,"english":"Thereat catching the dart of resistless course as it descended from the sky, the powerful monkey snapped it and then shouted.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.942,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058032","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"813d424e6f3fcf23c211e4fee8449085e26415adad1ca9a82cfbfaccbddf07d5","compact":"11900ea86a344704ed5c441acf778cd23b6afde9fb53a12ff02ace633fcb4ae7","nasal":"70120076620a319fc6a896974934a9a69622c40f96acb0f794083a90b7de254f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-33","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":33,"english":"Seeing that dreadful dart broken by Hanumān, the monkeys, transported with delignt, sent up shouts, even as clouds rumble.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.968,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058033","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e9714b95970df55f0b5c1d181e93dd83a4046b05c72f50047415d354137c6255","compact":"5d1c2bd9faad18225c214d1e73bb468ca6484234efea0e028f5cfe40f4b770d9","nasal":"5d1c2bd9faad18225c214d1e73bb468ca6484234efea0e028f5cfe40f4b770d9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-34","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":34,"english":"Then upraising his sword, that foremost of Raksasas-Trisiras-brought it down on the breast of the monkey-chief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.578,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058034","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fb63e2c12b25b61f71eb3d0e832483a2878fcc66638931c2aed03494f88e6ad8","compact":"582e8f158d01813b8224da80b7998fc4b64b63bd597e84beeb13cdac9dc24939","nasal":"3036c2d0dffc7d4844c1702c1db6c3cc1ffb4dae086202fbe219932df20d8574"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-35","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":35,"english":"Overpowered with the sword-blow, Hanumān son to the wind-god, endowed with energy, dealt the three-headed one a slap on the head.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.967,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058035","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bd1acabb1bf17176a41a65ae01951791504f868e06ccc035e40ab20ce7152fb3","compact":"1d54540d84af2ff2548645abb4345056391ed040b11e664c2ce4b2b23ab94229","nasal":"1d54540d84af2ff2548645abb4345056391ed040b11e664c2ce4b2b23ab94229"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-36","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":36,"english":"And smitten with that slap, the highly powerful Triśiras, with his hands and attire dropping off, fell down to the earth, deprived of consciousness.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.951,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058036","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2eee9698bbff90fb6f9e8f537beda2e7c216939d1a14d7114e4a9db2c78ef0d9","compact":"562845da920f74facdbce0ba94d580c20c52cad24aefdba9a7346823664ef07a","nasal":"06da6be6a93c29fdef329b2f1b41dc2f1050dde9a1a9311d33ae4f9bb6bc52b9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-37","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":37,"english":"Then that mighty monkey-resembling a hill broke his sword as he fell, and roared, terrifying all the Raksasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.661,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058037","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d74d1a1ba213a015dd14c4c1dcb76ea8f40a435ab1aa994737051a07b2e99589","compact":"74ab68d06bf2ea62b61ec4b9ce31a16e2dcc8a13959aba0b4ee12f939a06f6ee","nasal":"74ab68d06bf2ea62b61ec4b9ce31a16e2dcc8a13959aba0b4ee12f939a06f6ee"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-38","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":38,"english":"But not brooking that uproar, that night-ranger sprang up; and springing up, he dealt a blow at Hanuman.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058038","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"49f45399a9dd207d4ae4166b22c0c1a6c559a416e30323dac9b4d3cbe67c496f","compact":"c3fee466140fc177e13e97ccb43c17cd0c193269b8aca24e36c4e51672df1041","nasal":"27148ec3a25b1362ebcd97fce2104480dc1123e75a0b65e942e88f73941d3b27"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-39","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":39,"english":"At that blow, the redoubtable monkey was wrought up with wrath; and inflamed with rage, he smote that foremost of Räkşasas about his diadem.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058039","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"58c1a003b2478c9e75290d583f1a0f85770e7eba414dcda801feaf8cf10a0a00","compact":"92746de59507fba4b2cd42fac4996c300f522e560c5cd053806ec1c4c1932a92","nasal":"92746de59507fba4b2cd42fac4996c300f522e560c5cd053806ec1c4c1932a92"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-40","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":40,"english":"Then with a sharp sword the wind-god's son cut off his heads decked with diadems and furnished with ear-rings; even as Sakra had severed the heads of Tastri' son.* *Visvarupa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.916,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-42"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058040","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"33b5f8c33b08fc6c8e554c6892037a221d04fdd5a1f0289be31470bb78c6ea8b","compact":"8a1e4ab188e8959e63400c3512f6ca309aea1f4e05884d044bcbe8c0060c50a5","nasal":"94aee2841c9dff009bd10161718e0c4c2d45c18f931af488988cec2b3a5dacf6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-41","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":41,"english":"Thereat even as burning stars, loosened, drop down from the course of Indra, the large organs of sense, and eyes flaming like glowing fire, and heads of that foe of Indra, dropped down to the ground.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.775,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-43"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058041","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"42027daedee4881a8fe04d9ca574bbc3d28a635fc5a5563c949e421268e3ca79","compact":"74515c8580584390246ab2e8092b2ecae7e1beb4a8c86f0e40ddea297060941e","nasal":"22dd3193617c04fba64ba4169e3dcbc13d3374f7960428077a0bacb5a3213f91"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-42","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":42,"english":"On Trisiras, enemy of the immortals-having been slain by Hanuman endowed with the prowess itself of Sakra, the monkeys shouted, the earth shook, and the Rākṣas began to fly on all sides.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.835,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-44"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058042","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"87a71c65fdcbe0e053d6601c85184f4a525f6f8a3384185eacb6c1bd0fc83621","compact":"c9f71131a349aff63337d6728eb7bf245c43c887b3364292147de029e234214d","nasal":"bb0c1de10bcb6693eb716387a5878506ae3b5c3b181310e6844d4af8d486131e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-43","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":43,"english":"Seeing Triſira and Yuddhonmatta slain and seeing also the irrepressible Devāntaka and Narāntaka slain (in the encounter), that highly irascible and powerful Räkşasas-Matta, was transported with passion, and then took up a flaming mace entirely wrought with iron inlaid with gold; frothy with flesh and gore; mighty to behold; gratified with the blood of foes; with its end flaming in splendour; decked with red wreaths; and capable of striking terror into Airāvata and Mahāpadma and Sárvabhauma.* And flaming up like the fire arisen at the end of a Yuga, that foremost of Raksasas-Matta, wrought with fury, rushed against the monkeys. *Elephants of the cardinal points.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.565,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-70-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6058043","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"90d7faffa8500541aad7168ef5eb46427cff4fe561d354b9fc60bfa367139e11","compact":"c70c885d9de1421f149d928c6dbf4f5599ddc5edccfadd2663b51c95f6e2f14b","nasal":"c1d587d19e62c6386f66167787e57286a0980ebc110cc5a6adef41ef906065ad"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-58-44","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":58,"verse":44,"english":"Seeing Triſira and Yuddhonmatta slain and seeing also the irrepressible Devāntaka and Narāntaka slain (in the encounter), that highly irascible and powerful Räkşasas-Matta, was transported with passion, and then took up a flaming mace entirely wrought with iron inlaid with gold; frothy with flesh and gore; mighty to behold; gratified with the blood of foes; with its end flaming in splendour; decked with red wreaths; and capable of striking terror into Airāvata and Mahāpadma and Sárvabhauma.* And flaming up like the fire arisen at the end of a Yuga, that foremost of Raksasas-Matta, wrought with fury, rushed against the monkeys. *Elephants of the cardinal points.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence